---
description: HomeSpan-specific rules (HomeKit on ESP32)
globs: *.cpp, *.h, *.ino
alwaysApply: false
---

# HomeSpan Basics
- `homeSpan.poll()` must run in loop() on every iteration – nothing may block it
- All accessories/services are defined in setup() AFTER `homeSpan.begin()`
- Follow the HomeSpan structure: SpanAccessory → Service → Characteristic
- Custom services derive from the matching `Service::...` class;
  react to HomeKit writes in `update()`, return true/false correctly
- Periodic work belongs in the service's `loop()` method, non-blocking,
  millis()-based

# Characteristics
- Only update characteristics via `setVal()` when the value actually changed
  (avoids unnecessary HomeKit notifications)
- Read current values with `getVal()` / `getNewVal()` inside update()
- Respect valid ranges of HAP characteristics (e.g. brightness 0-100)

# WiFi & Setup
- Use `homeSpan.enableAutoStartAP()` for first-time WiFi provisioning
- Never hardcode WiFi credentials in the sketch – they live in NVS
- Pairing code: 8 digits, set via `homeSpan.setPairingCode()` or serial 'S' command;
  never use blacklisted codes (12345678, 87654321, all-same-digit)
- ESP32-C3 is 2.4 GHz only – do not suggest 5 GHz features

# Flash / Partitions
- Sketch requires a large app partition: "Minimal SPIFFS (1.9MB APP with OTA)"
  or "Huge APP (3MB No OTA)" – keep this in mind for OTA decisions
- If OTA is used: `homeSpan.enableOTA()` and the OTA-capable partition scheme

# Stability
- Status LED and control button via `homeSpan.setStatusPin()` /
  `homeSpan.setControlPin()` instead of custom implementations
- Log via `homeSpan.setLogLevel()` / WEBLOG, not via scattered Serial.print
- NVS writes are flash writes – do not write cyclically/frequently
  (flash wear); persist only on real changes
